0.12 0.12 0.12 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 628.19 Td (A Git branch reference is a single pointer \(refs/heads/<branch>\) to a commit hash. When commits) Tj ET
0.12 0.12 0.12 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 614.69 Td (occur, Git writes a new commit object and advances the ref. If two active worktrees shared one) Tj ET
0.12 0.12 0.12 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 601.19 Td (branch, each would maintain its own staging index and working tree. Simultaneous commits would) Tj ET
0.12 0.12 0.12 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 587.69 Td (create race conditions, silently overwriting branch updates or desynchronizing HEAD, corrupting) Tj ET
0.12 0.12 0.12 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 574.19 Td (local repository state.) Tj ET
0.20 0.40 0.80 rg
